Using the synthesized parameters, the total antenna array is designed based on the single element radiator described in \cref{sec:element_design}. An exploded view of the \ac{M3PA} array stack-up in multi-layer \ac{PCB} technology is shown in \cref{fig:array_exploded}. The \ac{PCB} consists of a total number of ten layers with the transmission lines integrated in stripline technology. The radiating antenna aperture is located on the highest layer of the \ac{PCB} with the excitation feeds of the antenna element located on the layers beneath it. A breakout layer is positioned beneath the feed networks to route and distribute the input signals to the individual antenna elements. The input signals are fed to the \ac{PCB} using $8\times1$ connectors from the Rosenberger Mini-Coax Multi-Port series, which are located on the bottom side of the \ac{PCB}.
